  "expected_answer": "functional skipped (signed-in check), context pass, load pass, accessibility FAIL: brand colour #FFE680 on white has a contrast of about 1.3:1, needs 4.5:1; responsiveness not run (pending). alpha_app is now reverted and a fix task was filed.",
  "final_text": "The tests on alpha_app failed. The accessibility lane failed, so the suite stopped there, set alpha_app to **reverted**, and filed task **mold_v1-009**.\n\n| Lane | Result | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Functional | skipped | 2 of 3 checks passed. `chat.turn` didn't run because it needs a signed-in session. |\n| Context | **pass** | 1 of 1 |\n| Load | **pass** | 1 of 1 |\n| Accessibility | **fail** | `brand.contrast` failed. `authenticated.surface` didn't run because it needs a signed-in session. |\n| Responsiveness | not run | The run stopped at the accessibility failure, so this lane is back to `pending`. |\n\n**Why it failed:** alpha_app's brand colour is a pale yellow, `#FFE680`. Against white it has a contrast of 1.2:1, and buttons and links need at least 4.5:1 to be readable (the WCAG AA accessibility standard). The colour is set as `brand_color` (and `icon_bg`) in `state/application/alpha_app/application.json:239`. The fix is a brand decision: either pick a darker brand colour, or keep the yellow as an accent and use a darker colour for buttons and links. I haven't changed anything. Tell me which colour you want and I'll update it and run the tests again.\n\n**Even with the colour fixed, the tests can't fully pass yet.** Three checks need to sign in as a real person: one in functional, one in accessibility, and the responsiveness checks. They need someone who can sign in to receive a one-time code by email. Sending that email requires your go-ahead, so tell me whose email to use when you want those checks covered.\n\nFull report: `molds/mold_v1/testing/accessibility/reports/alpha_app-2026-10-09T135254Z.md`\n\nThese results came from the factory's rehearsal checks, graded against a stand-in deployment, not a real live site.",
